PUBLIC RESPONSE: {} 

After examining the five empty points that are adjacent to Black, none of them gives White a forced capture.

* A1 and A3 are immediately lost to Black capture;
* B2 is played with only the liberty B1 and is captured on the next move by B1, so the move is a self-capture in effect;
* B1 puts C1-C2 in atari but Black can answer B2. B2 joins A2-B3-C2-C1 into one large Black group with liberties A1 A3 A4 and puts the newly played White B1 in atari on A1. A1 cannot be played to save B1 because A1+B1 would be a suicide with no capture, so White loses B1.
* A4 does not create an atari and Black can reply B2 and then A1 to keep the large group alive and to keep White’s A4 atariable.

With best play Black can always keep at least one liberty on every Black group, so White has no first move that forces a kill.

